; int-sum-fold: the SIGNED-integer accumulator fold, proven correct for EVERY input list — the ℤ analogue of
; sum-forall and the first ∀-input correctness proof over SIGNED integers (difference-pair ℤ). Matches the exact
; shape of recursive_sum's `sum(s[1..], acc + s[0])` machine (ACC-FIRST accumulation). listsum/sumfold run over a
; list of BUNDLED integers (k 70 a b); the theorem is up to ~ (intEq). Goal: forall xs acc. intEq(intAdd(acc,
; listsum xs), sumfold(xs, acc)). Nil: identity-bundled. Cons: rearrange acc+(h+lt) ~ (acc+h)+lt via sym(assoc),
; then trans with IH@(acc+h). The bundled-ℤ lemmas (identity/assoc/sym/trans, lifted from the component ZZ
; library by prodrec and inlined here as defs) are ∀ over ABSTRACT integers, so the fold cites them on the
; abstract head/tail directly — no prodrec needed in the fold itself.
